sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 5 of the command pipeline (feature-flow "The VM job"). A CI job on the beast or shark runner calls orbit proof:run COMMIT and reports the required check Proofs. The inside of proof:run is the chart proof.run; this chart shows the CI side around it.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: pipeline stage 5 · VM CI
  %% kind: pipeline.5-vm-ci
  autonumber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=PR tone=blue
  %% lane RN icon=terminal pill=CI job tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>PR · merge queue
  participant RN as CI job<br/>beast · shark
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>one parent run
  participant VM as Proof task VM<br/>nested fleet
  GH->>RN: Start Proofs<br/>PR head or queue commit
  %%> Triggers:
  %%> - a PR from a branch of the repository runs it automatically; the merge queue runs it on the combined commit
  %%> - a fork PR starts nothing by itself
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - the CI job on the self-hosted runners and the required check `Proofs`
  Note over RN: Scope the change<br/>bin/proof-select from main
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - a hosted step reads the changed paths with the selection list of `main`, not of the PR
  %%> - a path that matches no line fails the step; a documentation-only change never starts the VM job
  opt the PR is from outside
    GH->>RN: Review + run-proofs label<br/>maintainer
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a maintainer approves the head and adds the label `run-proofs`; the workflow passes that head SHA to `proof:run`
    %%> - it reports the verdict as the commit status `Proofs`, then runs the failed `Proofs` job again
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a new push removes the label; the new head needs a new approval
  end
  RN->>GW: proof:run COMMIT<br/>+ idempotency key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - passes only the full SHA and a key built from the workflow run and attempt; checks out nothing and chooses no cases
  %%> - passes no secret; reaches the Gateway over the private network
  Note over GW: Check and select<br/>trusted commit · cases
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - refuses a commit that is not on a branch of the repository, or an outside PR without review and label
  %%> - selects the cases from the diff and the selection list; nothing to prove ends here as a skip
  %%> - detail in the chart `proof.run`
  GW->>SW: Start one run<br/>operation-proof-run
  %%> Built:
  %%> - the admission, the trust check, the case selection, and a Gateway-started chain that runs the proof; off by default (`proof.execution`)
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - the one Swamp flow that replaces the chain; the receipt store
  SW->>VM: Provision, verify, destroy<br/>three child workflows
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - provision per stage 2, verify per stage 3, destroy always; the VM holds no Pi token and no model key
  %%> Budget:
  %%> - 30 minutes after the fleet is ready
  VM-->>SW: Verdict per case
  %%> Result:
  %%> - one verdict per selected case; a failed or unexecuted case fails the run, then the VM is destroyed
  loop until the run ends
    RN->>GW: operation:show TASK
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the job reads the task until it ends; the Gateway projects the result once, from the run
    GW-->>RN: status + verdicts
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the status and the verdicts, with no command output and no host name
  end
  RN->>GH: Report Proofs<br/>pass or fail
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the job exits with the verdict and writes a summary: each case, the uncovered paths, the receipt link
  %%> - a run with uncovered paths and no case passes, and the summary says so
  %%> - timeout 45 minutes; a cancelled job cancels its run
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - `Proofs` as a required status of the merge ruleset, next to `Required checks`; only the scope step may skip it
  alt Proofs and Required checks pass
    Note over GH: Queue lands the PR<br/>stage 4 continues
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the merge queue takes the PR, and tests the combined commit with the same selection
  else a case fails or did not run
    Note over GH: Block the merge<br/>PR stays out of the queue
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the author fixes the change; a missing result or a failed assertion fails the check
  end
